+- White paper and near-black ink remain the canvas. Volt highlights selections and primary actions; vermilion marks caveats. Semantic status colors always have accompanying words or icons.
+- Volt never appears as text on paper or as the sole boundary on white. Use an ink label and ink boundary on volt fills; catch text uses accessible vermilion text tokens.
+- The sticker device may appear once per page. Pills are allowed for buttons and filter chips; 24–32 px radii are allowed on hero surfaces. Dense comparison surfaces keep clear row rules and restrained rounding.
